cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "EleutherIA: An AI-Powered Scholarly Research Platform for Ancient Philosophy on Free Will"
message: "If you use this software or dataset, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Girardi
    given-names: Romain
    email: romain.girardi@univ-cotedazur.fr
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5310-5346"
    affiliation: "Universite Cote d'Azur, CEPAM; Universite de Geneve, Faculte de Theologie Jean Calvin"
repository-code: "https://github.com/romain-girardi-eng/EleutherIA"
url: "https://free-will.app"
abstract: >-
  EleutherIA is an open scholarly research platform and FAIR-aligned
  knowledge graph for ancient debates on free will, fate, moral
  responsibility, and agency across the Greco-Roman and early Christian
  worlds. This release combines a curated knowledge graph, an ancient-text
  corpus, and an agentic GraphRAG stack for citation-grounded question
  answering, graph exploration, and data quality auditing. As of the
  2026-03-10 audit bundled with this release, the live graph contains 17,396
  nodes, 42,161 edges, and 13,293 passage citations; the broader platform
  indexes 487 ancient works and more than 69,000 passages in Greek, Latin,
  English, Hebrew, and Arabic.
